    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **James Wood** (78.42) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against Zack Littell and J.T. Ginn, respectively. **James Wood** is our premier play, buoyed by an elite 0.437 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot, while **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) offer significant value due to favorable park factors and high-end platoon advantages. The lineup's aggressive configuration prioritizes these efficiency surges, specifically targeting pitchers with xERAs near 5.00 to maximize our offensive output. **Corbin Carroll** (70.40) remains a lock, as his game-changing stolen base potential provides necessary upside even against the tougher arm of Dustin May.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Seiya Suzuki** (57.43), who sits just shy of the preferred starting threshold despite a solid projection. While **Seiya Suzuki** presents a respectable floor, the optimizer favored **Gabriel Moreno** (57.04) and **Isaac Paredes** (59.35) due to their specific batting order utility and the favorable park dynamics currently favoring our corner infielders. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Zach McKinstry**, **Henry Bolte**, **James Wood**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**; should any of these players move down in the order upon official release, their efficiency scores will slide, potentially triggering a last-minute shift toward **Austin Riley** (52.82) to maintain our category floor. We continue to hold **Travis Bazzana** in reserve, as his projected output remains suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against Montgomery.",
